Single-precision PW RT-TDDFT for H2 with a nonzero electric field.

A 40-Bohr cubic cell and a Gamma-centered 2x1x1 mesh provide two k pools for
the two-rank GPU driver. The molecule has a 1.4-Bohr bond. Atomic initial
orbitals, two bands, an 8-Ry wavefunction cutoff, and explicit convergence thresholds
reduce initialization and roundoff sensitivity. The Hartree and XC potentials
remain self-consistent; no Hamiltonian terms are disabled. The electric-field
amplitude is 0.1 V/Angstrom, giving a resolvable response in the dilute cell.
The current comparison retains the standard absolute tolerance of 1e-10;
the existing threshold file sets the energy tolerance to 1e-4 eV.

Fixed ions with zero velocities; pw_seed=1 and explicit initialization controls.
Nine electronic samples cover 0.00--0.08 fs. Compare final energy and current_tot.txt
with the existing Autotest.sh and CompareFile.py tolerances. Forces and stress are
not reference observables. GPU references are copied unchanged from the CPU case.

References were generated with 4 MPI ranks and 2 OpenMP threads on CPU;
the GPU mirror is checked with 2 MPI ranks and 2 OpenMP threads. No GPU-specific
reference or current-comparison tolerance is used.
A matching double-precision trajectory was checked before accepting the reference.
